<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">HUMAN GOLD RUSH LESSON</p><h1>Three Ways to Respond</h1><p class="intro">Human Gold Rush encounters are invitations, not conversion funnels.</p><blockquote>Can a community learn equally from yes, not yet, and no?</blockquote></header><section class="content-grid"><article><span>01</span><div><h2>Participate</h2><p>Accept the invitation and take an active role in the community experience.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h2>Observe</h2><p>Remain present, learn, and decide in your own time without pressure to perform.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h2>Walk away</h2><p>Decline freely. Re-entry remains open. The response is recorded only within the person’s consent.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h2>Walk-away gold</h2><p>A walk-away can reveal where relevance, clarity, access, timing, or trust has not formed. Record the outcome—never invent the motive.</p></div></article><article><span>05</span><div><h2>Curiosity remains supreme</h2><p>Participate, observe, or walk away — every response is read as data, not a verdict. Curiosity about what actually happened outranks any pressure to convert, judge, or explain it away. When a motive isn’t known, the honest entry is “not yet known,” never a guess dressed up as certainty.</p></div></article></section><section class="media-section"><div class="section-heading"><p>MEDIA FOR THIS LESSON</p><h2>Watch, listen, and discuss</h2></div><div class="media-grid"><article class="media-card video"><div class="media-frame"><span>▶</span><small>VIDEO 1</small></div><h3>Three Ways to Respond: orientation</h3><p>Reserved for the featured story or introductory video.</p><a href="#">Transcript coming soon</a></article><article class="media-card video"><div class="media-frame"><span>▶</span><small>VIDEO 2</small></div><h3>Community conversation</h3><p>Reserved for a demonstration, conversation, or local example.</p><a href="#">Discussion guide coming soon</a></article><article class="media-card podcast"><div class="media-frame"><span>◉</span><small>PODCAST</small></div><h3>Listen and reflect</h3><p>Reserved for the facilitator or community podcast episode.</p><a href="#">Transcript coming soon</a></article></div></section>
